In previous versions of (net)hack the '/' command was sufficient, since it
wasn't needed so much. Now that 3.0 has come, I frequently find myself typing:
	'/'
	Specify unknown object by cursor? [ynq]
	'y'
	Please move the cursor to the unknown object. --more--
	'space'
	(for instructions type a ?)

This is ANNOYING folks! When you enter a room full of unknown monsters,
you enter the same sequence for all monsters! 

Why couldn't it be like this:
	'/'
	(for instructions type a ?)

The identification by letter could be assigned to another key..
